p.d=A.b([new A.h1("AppHear",B.dm,B.dr,o,"AppHear is an iOS app that I helped develop, to help deaf students review lectures through media playback features. Using AVFoundation and AVKit, I implemented a feature to save and play media files, allowing students to easily access recorded lectures. The app includes features like adjustable playback speed and captions, enhancing accessibility for students. I also applied the MVVM design pattern to improve code modularity and ensure the app is easy to maintain and scale.","SwiftUI, AVFoundation, Core Data, List, Slider, Fonts, Audio Visualizer, Overlay, Segmented Control, Alert",!0,"iOS","assets/apphear/apphear_logo.png",f),new A.h1("Totally",B.dm,B.dr,n,"For Totally, a personal finance tracking app, I built a solution that lets users track their credit card expenses and categorize them into various spending categories. The app allows users to connect their bank accounts, retrieve transaction data, and generate monthly reports. I developed this app using SwiftUI, Core Data, and CloudKit to ensure smooth data synchronization across devices. The app also features budgeting tools and expense breakdowns to give users insight into their spending patterns.","SwiftUI, Core Data, Charts, Data Visualization",!0,"iOS","assets/totally/totally_logo.png",f),new A.h1("OWL Launcher",B.dm,B.dr,m,"I developed the OWL Launcher for plantation workers, using Flutter to create a custom launcher that restricts device access to authorized apps, ensuring the devices are only used for work-related purposes. Key features include kiosk mode, device admin controls, and widgets for battery, weather, and date. The app helps improve productivity and reduces distractions, with a focus on creating an easy-to-use interface and seamless functionality. I also integrated API calls to ensure up-to-date weather and battery information.","GetX state management, Android System APIs, Shared Preferences, Kiosk Mode, Google Maps API, Material Design.",!0,"Flutter",u.X,f),new A.h1("UENA",B.dm,B.dr,l,"At UENA, I contributed to the development of an intuitive food ordering app for both iOS and Android. I implemented several key features, including a voucher feature to allow users to redeem discounts, and a pop-up feature to notify users of special offers and promotions. I also developed update prompts to notify users of app updates, ensuring they stay up-to-date with the latest features and improvements. Additionally, I introduced a stamps feature that rewarded users for frequent purchases, enhancing user engagement and retention. Using Xcode and Android Studio, I worked on optimizing app performance, fixing bugs, and improving the overall user experience across both platforms.","UIKit, SnapKit, Swift, Kotlin, App Development Cycle, Performance Tuning, Retrofit, OkHttp, Typescript, Google Play Console, App Store Connect",!0,"Android, iOS","assets/uena/uenafood_logo.jpeg",f),new A.h1("Xpiry",B.dm,B.dr,r,"I created Xpiry, an iOS app built with SwiftUI, that helps users track the expiration dates of household items. The app allows users to save images of items and set reminders for when they are about to expire. I implemented features such as stock management using Core Data and Steppers for counting items. The app also incorporates PhotosUI to allow users to pick images from their device gallery, creating a seamless and intuitive experience for managing household inventory.","SwiftUI, Image Picker, Core Data, List, Progress Bar, NSFetchRequest, Search, Overlay, Segmented Control, Alert, Action Sheet",!0,"iOS","assets/xpiry/xpiry_logo.png",f),new A.h1("Messages",B.nr,B.JY,f,f,f,!1,f,f,"https://wa.me/628121162001"),new A.h1(k,B.Fa,i,f,f,f,!1,f,j,"mailto:jasonkenneth17@gmail.com"),new A.h1(h,B.F9,B.dq,f,f,f,!1,f,q,"https://www.google.com/search"),new A.h1("LinkedIn",B.dm,B.BY,f,f,f,!1,f,"assets/logos/linkedin_logo.png","https://www.linkedin.com/in/jasonkenneth/")],s)
